# Cloud agent — Character Animation Tuner

When tuning or verifying limb/animation presets on a **Cursor Cloud agent** (no Godot editor window):

## Default commands (repo root)

```bash
bash tools/run_limb_tuner.sh verify
```

Runs headless: `test_limb_tuner.gd`, `test_limb_bake.gd`, and tuner smoke. Logs → `Tests/logs/`.

```bash
bash tools/run_limb_tuner.sh bake --weapon none --clip idle
```

Bakes PNG+JSON from on-disk `.tres` presets (no GUI).

```bash
bash tools/run_limb_tuner.sh share-web
```

Starts the **web card tuner** and prints a share link (cloudflared) so the human can preview in a browser.

## Godot binary

Set **`GODOT=/path/to/Godot`** if `godot` / `godot4` is not on PATH. Cloud Linux VMs need a downloaded Godot 4.x binary (standard or headless build).

## Do not

- Tell the user to open `LimbTuner.tscn` and press F6 as the **only** verification on cloud — run `verify` or `bake` yourself.
- Use `gui` mode without `DISPLAY` — it will fail by design.

## Human visual review

- **Browser:** `share-web` (limited schema — walk/attack extras need Godot tuner).
- **Desktop:** user runs `bash tools/run_limb_tuner.sh gui` locally.

